Subject: Propose changes as a pull request instead of naming write tools

Why: A change to a cluster or Google Cloud resource goes out as a pull request in the GitOps repository's format, never as a direct write; the gke MCP server offers read tools only (#2955) and the broker refuses kubectl and gcloud writes, so instructions naming write tools or write commands point the agent at paths it does not have and away from the pull request (#2935). A node pool's version change is the one exception: a `spec.version` in the repository pins a release-channel pool against auto-upgrade (`bench/tf/fleet/main.tf` documents the same fight in Terraform), so the patch keeps the `gcloud container clusters upgrade --node-pool` command as a step for the platform operator rather than a pull request.
Local-Issue: #3185
Upstream-Issue: none (specific to this repository)
Retire-When: never; kube-agents proposes every change as a pull request, or a node pool's version change as a platform-operator step

